            "contentType": "VIDEO",
            "title": "How to play cruise stocks in a a K-shaped economy",
            "description": "<p>There are growing concerns about the consumer, with many saying <a data-i13n=\"cpos:1;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/personal-finance/banking/article/what-is-a-k-shaped-economy-and-whats-causing-the-divide-213458866.html\">there is a \"K-shaped economy\"</a> where the wealthiest are spending more while the lower end is pulling back. So what does that mean for leisure spending on things like cruises?  Citi leisure & travel analyst James Hardiman explains how to play the cruise industry right now. He also explains why he likes motor sports company BRP (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:2;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/DOO\">DOO</a>).</p>\n<p>To watch more expert insights and analysis on the latest market action, check out more <a data-i13n=\"cpos:3;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/videos/series/market-catalysts/\">Market Catalysts</a>.</p>",
